257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Aim :  Develop an accurate, reliable, and generalizable machine learning model to estimate the fouling factor \(Rf\) in heat exchangers based on operational parameters, in order to improve energy efficiency, reduce maintenance costs, and enable predictive cleaning.)
/E (Aim :  Develop an accurate, reliable, and generalizable machine learning model to estimate the fouling factor \(Rf\) in heat exchangers based on operational parameters, in order to improve energy efficiency, reduce maintenance costs, and enable predictive cleaning.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Background : Fouling in heat exchangers, including MSFE heaters, is the buildup of unwanted materials like scale or corrosion on surfaces, reducing heat transfer efficiency. The fouling factor \(Rf\) is a key performance metric representing thermal resistance caused by fouling. Traditionally, Rf is estimated using simplified empirical formulas, but these often fail under dynamic and non-linear industrial conditions. The paper proposes using machine learning for accurate and robust Rf prediction to help industries optimize cleaning schedules and reduce energy loss.)
/E (Background : Fouling in heat exchangers, including MSFE heaters, is the buildup of unwanted materials like scale or corrosion on surfaces, reducing heat transfer efficiency. The fouling factor \(Rf\) is a key performance metric representing thermal resistance caused by fouling. Traditionally, Rf is estimated using simplified empirical formulas, but these often fail under dynamic and non-linear industrial conditions. The paper proposes using machine learning for accurate and robust Rf prediction to help industries optimize cleaning schedules and reduce energy loss.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
